From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a mouse's unaccelerated motion reaches the shell

zwp_relative_pointer_v1 carries a device's motion twice: accelerated,
as the cursor moved, and unaccelerated, which games and VM viewers read
for aiming. On a console the engine reads mice through libinput, which
reports both. LibInputEventConverter passes the unaccelerated deltas as
the move's ordinal_delta, EventFactoryEvdev keeps them on the MouseEvent
as an event property (ui/events/domicile/unaccelerated_motion.h), and
MakeWebMouseEvent copies them into WebPointerProperties. They cross to
the renderer in PointerData, add up when moves coalesce, and reach the
<app> element on the PointerEvent, which hands them to the shell's
DomicileHost. A move no device made carries none.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
